---
alwaysApply: true
---

Never use FindObjectOfType
Never use null propagation
Where possible spawn GameObjects in using Addressables, not Prefab Instantiation
Don't generate .meta files, let Unity create them
Never use UnityEngine.Input
Never use System.Threading.Tasks for gameplay unless asked
Keep method calls on one line when they fit; do not wrap with one argument per line (e.g. `ApplyAndPlay( a, b, c, d, e, f );` not each arg on its own line). Only break lines when a call genuinely exceeds readable length.
Do not edit .unity scene files
Do not create Ensure / Setup editor scripts that destroy-and-recreate scene objects or prefabs. Author scene and prefab changes in the Editor (or via Unity MCP GameObject/component edits). One-shot bootstrap code is only allowed when it creates a missing asset once and never stomps existing scene/prefab authoring on re-run.
Never use — (em dash) anywhere, plans, code, anything